🎤 Interview Questions

What is Spring Data JPA Auditing?
It automatically tracks entity metadata such as creation time, modification time, creator, and last modifier.

What does @CreatedDate do?
Automatically stores the entity's creation timestamp.

What does @LastModifiedDate do?
Tracks when the entity was last modified.

What does @EnableJpaAuditing do?
Enables Spring Data JPA auditing support.

What is AuditorAware?
It provides information about the current auditor, commonly the authenticated user, for fields such as @CreatedBy and @LastModifiedBy.

Why use a BaseEntity?
To centralize common audit fields and avoid duplicating them across multiple entities.

